' Combined source for local rendering. For web rendering, use one of the
' individual diagrams in docs/sequence-diagrams/ to keep request URLs small.
@startuml
title JKsur+ Sequence 1 - Admin and Staff Sign In and Sign Out

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #222222
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #777777
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444444
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8E8F0
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #222222

actor "Admin / Staff" as User
participant "Web App" as App
participant "Sign-In Modal" as SignIn
participant "Store Context" as Store
participant "Supabase Auth" as Auth

User -> App: Open web application
App --> User: Display public shop
User -> App: Choose Staff / Owner Sign In
App -> SignIn: Open sign-in modal
User -> SignIn: Enter email and password
SignIn -> SignIn: Validate email and password format
SignIn -> Store: loginAs(email, password)
Store -> Auth: signInWithPassword(email, password)

alt Credentials rejected
  Auth --> Store: Authentication error
  Store --> SignIn: Return error
  SignIn --> User: Display sign-in error
  User -> SignIn: Correct credentials and retry
else Credentials accepted
  Auth --> Store: Authenticated user and role metadata
  Store -> Store: Determine app role from email and metadata
  Store -> App: Set authenticated user
  alt Owner / admin account
    App -> App: Select Dashboard as default view
    App --> User: Display admin dashboard and admin navigation
  else Staff account
    App -> App: Select POS as default view
    App --> User: Display staff navigation and POS
  else Other authenticated account
    App -> App: Select public Showcase as default view
    App --> User: Display customer view
  end
end

User -> App: Select Sign Out
App -> Store: logout()
Store -> Auth: signOut()
alt Sign-out succeeds
  Auth --> Store: Session ended
  Store -> Store: Set current user to Guest
  Store -> Store: Remove cached user profile
  Store --> App: Sign-out complete
  App --> User: Show public shop navigation
else Sign-out fails
  Auth --> Store: Sign-out error
  Store --> App: Return error
  App --> User: Display sign-out failure alert
end
@enduml

@startuml
title JKsur+ Sequence 2 - Browse Showcase and Review Top Customers

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #222222
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #777777
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444444
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8E8F0
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #222222

actor "Visitor / Admin / Staff" as User
participant "Showcase View" as Shop
participant "Store Context" as Store
database "Supabase Database" as DB

note over Store,DB
The app subscribes to product, category, and order data when it starts.
The showcase filters this already-loaded data in the browser.
end note

Store -> DB: Read products, categories, and orders;\nsubscribe to realtime changes
DB --> Store: Initial rows and later data updates
User -> Shop: Open Browse Clothing
Shop -> Store: Read products and categories
Store --> Shop: Current product and category state
User -> Shop: Search, choose category,\nand/or set maximum price
Shop -> Shop: Filter products in memory
Shop --> User: Display matching products

opt Review top customers
  User -> Shop: Select Top 10 Customers
  Shop -> Shop: Choose month or custom date range
  Shop -> Shop: Aggregate non-cancelled orders\nand exclude walk-in customers
  Shop -> Shop: Sort by total spent and keep top ten
  Shop --> User: Display top customers for selected dates
end
@enduml

@startuml
title JKsur+ Sequence 3 - Inventory Management

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #222222
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #777777
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444444
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8E8F0
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #222222

actor "Admin / Staff" as User
participant "Inventory View" as Inventory
participant "Item Status Modal" as Modal
participant "Store Context" as Store
database "Supabase Database" as DB

User -> Inventory: Choose Suppliers, Categories,\nBales, or Products
Inventory -> Store: Read current inventory state
Store --> Inventory: Return selected records
User -> Inventory: Enter or edit record details
Inventory -> Inventory: Validate required fields

alt Add a record
  Inventory -> Store: addSupplier / addCategory /\naddBale / addProduct
  Store -> Store: Add record to local state
  Store -> DB: setDoc(collection, new record)
  DB --> Store: Write result
else Edit a record
  Inventory -> Store: updateSupplier / updateCategory /\nupdateBale / updateProduct
  Store -> Store: Update record in local state
  Store -> DB: updateDoc(record, changed fields)
  DB --> Store: Write result
else Delete a record
  Inventory --> User: Request deletion confirmation
  User -> Inventory: Confirm deletion
  Inventory -> Store: deleteSupplier / deleteCategory /\ndeleteBale / deleteProduct
  Store -> Store: Remove record from local state
  Store -> DB: deleteDoc(record)
  DB --> Store: Write result
end

Store --> Inventory: Publish updated state
Inventory --> User: Refresh inventory list

User -> Inventory: Choose Log Item Status
Inventory -> Modal: Open status form
User -> Modal: Select product, status, quantity,\nand optional notes
Modal -> Modal: Validate status details
Modal -> Store: logItemStatus(status details)
Store -> Store: Add status log to local state
Store -> DB: setDoc(item_logs, status log)
DB --> Store: Write result

opt Stock adjustment is enabled
  alt Item returned
    Store -> Store: Increase available quantity
  else Item damaged or lost
    Store -> Store: Decrease available quantity
  end
  Store -> DB: updateDoc(products, available quantity)
  DB --> Store: Write result
end

Store --> Inventory: Publish updated logs and stock
Inventory --> User: Display updated inventory

opt Mark a lost item as found
  User -> Inventory: Update lost-item log and restore quantity
  Inventory -> Store: updateItemStatusLog(restoreStock)
  Store -> DB: updateDoc(item_logs, changed status)
  Store -> Store: Add restored quantity to product stock
  Store -> DB: updateDoc(products, available quantity)
  DB --> Store: Write result
end
@enduml
@startuml
title JKsur+ Sequence 4 - Complete an In-Store POS Sale

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #222222
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #777777
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444444
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8E8F0
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #222222

actor "Admin / Staff" as User
participant "POS View" as POS
participant "Store Context" as Store
database "Supabase Database" as DB
participant "Receipt Modal" as Receipt
participant "Print Dialog" as Print

User -> POS: Search by product name or barcode
POS -> Store: Read product list
Store --> POS: Current products and stock quantities
User -> POS: Add products and set quantities
POS -> POS: Check availability and calculate subtotal
User -> POS: Enter customer, sale date,\ndiscount, payment method, and tendered amount
POS -> POS: Validate cart, discount, date,\nand sufficient payment

alt Invalid sale details or insufficient payment
  POS --> User: Display validation message
  User -> POS: Correct sale details
else Valid sale
  POS -> Store: completePosSale(cart and payment details)
  Store -> Store: Create completed order and order number
  Store -> Store: Reduce product quantities and update bale sales
  Store -> Store: Create sold item logs
  Store -> Store: Create POS sales inflow transaction
  Store -> DB: Write product, bale, and item-log updates
  Store -> DB: setDoc(orders, completed order)
  Store -> DB: setDoc(transactions, sales inflow)
  DB --> Store: Write results
  Store --> POS: Return completed order
  POS -> POS: Clear cart and sale form
  POS -> Receipt: Display receipt for completed order
  Receipt --> User: Show receipt, total, payment, and change
  opt Print receipt
    User -> Receipt: Select Print Receipt
    Receipt -> Print: Open browser print dialog
  end
end

note over Store,DB
The app issues separate database writes for sale, stock, logs, and inflow;
they are not wrapped in a single database transaction.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title JKsur+ Sequence 5 - Finance Management

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #222222
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #777777
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444444
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8E8F0
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #222222

actor "Admin" as User
participant "Finance View" as Finance
participant "Store Context" as Store
database "Supabase Database" as DB
participant "Browser" as Browser

User -> Finance: Open Expense Accounts
Finance -> Store: Read expense accounts
Store --> Finance: Current accounts and budgets
User -> Finance: Enter or edit account name,\nmonthly budget, and details
Finance -> Finance: Validate name and positive budget

alt Add account
  Finance -> Store: addExpenseAccount(account details)
  Store -> Store: Add account to local state
  Store -> DB: setDoc(expense_accounts, account)
else Edit account
  Finance -> Store: updateExpenseAccount(id, changes)
  Store -> Store: Update local account state
  Store -> DB: updateDoc(expense_accounts, changes)
else Delete account
  Finance --> User: Request deletion confirmation
  User -> Finance: Confirm deletion
  Finance -> Store: deleteExpenseAccount(id)
  Store -> Store: Remove account from local state
  Store -> DB: deleteDoc(expense_accounts, id)
end

DB --> Store: Write result
Store --> Finance: Publish updated accounts
Finance --> User: Display updated account list

User -> Finance: Open Record Expense
Finance -> Store: Read expense accounts
Store --> Finance: Available accounts and budgets
User -> Finance: Enter account, amount, date,\npayment method, description
opt Attach receipt image
  User -> Finance: Select image
  Finance -> Browser: Read image as data URL
  Browser --> Finance: Receipt image data
end
Finance -> Finance: Validate account and positive amount
Finance -> Store: addExpense(expense details)
Store -> Store: Create expense and matching outflow transaction
Store -> DB: setDoc(expenses, expense)
Store -> DB: setDoc(transactions, outflow)
DB --> Store: Write results
Store --> Finance: Publish expense and transaction
Finance --> User: Switch to Transaction History

User -> Finance: Search, filter, or export transaction history
Finance -> Finance: Filter current transaction data\nor generate spreadsheet download
Finance --> User: Display results or download export

opt Delete a transaction
  User -> Finance: Select delete and confirm
  Finance -> Store: deleteTransaction(transaction id)
  Store -> DB: deleteDoc(transactions, id)
  opt Transaction is linked to an expense or order
    Store -> DB: deleteDoc(linked expense or order)
  end
  DB --> Store: Write results
  Store --> Finance: Publish updated history
  Finance --> User: Display updated transactions
end
@enduml

@startuml
title JKsur+ Sequence 6 - View Dashboard

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #222222
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #777777
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444444
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8E8F0
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #222222

actor "Admin" as User
participant "Dashboard View" as View
participant "Store Context" as Store
database "Supabase Database" as DB

note over Store,DB
On application startup, Store Context loads the dashboard data from
Supabase and subscribes to Realtime changes.
end note

Store -> DB: SELECT * FROM orders
Store -> DB: SELECT * FROM transactions
Store -> DB: SELECT * FROM products
Store -> DB: SELECT * FROM expenses
DB --> Store: Return order, transaction,\nproduct, and expense rows
Store -> Store: Map database rows and update app state
DB --> Store: Push later Realtime table changes
Store -> Store: Refresh state from changed database rows

User -> View: Open Dashboard
View -> Store: Read current orders, transactions,\nexpenses, customers, and products
Store --> View: Return loaded dashboard data
User -> View: Select date range
View -> View: Filter data and calculate sales,\nexpenses, profit, assets, and customer metrics
View --> User: Display dashboard KPIs and charts
@enduml

@startuml
title JKsur+ Sequence 7 - View Sales Forecast

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #222222
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #777777
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444444
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8E8F0
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #222222

actor "Admin" as User
participant "Sales Forecast View" as Forecast
participant "Store Context" as Store
database "Supabase Database" as DB

note over Store,DB
On application startup, Store Context fetches sales orders,
transactions, and products from Supabase and subscribes to Realtime
updates. The forecast uses the loaded and updated records.
end note

Store -> DB: SELECT * FROM orders
Store -> DB: SELECT * FROM transactions
Store -> DB: SELECT * FROM products
DB --> Store: Return order, transaction,\nand product rows
Store -> Store: Map database rows and update app state
DB --> Store: Push later Realtime table changes
Store -> Store: Refresh state from changed database rows

User -> Forecast: Open Sales Forecast
User -> Forecast: Choose product category\nand forecast horizon
Forecast -> Store: Read current orders,\ntransactions, and products
Store --> Forecast: Return loaded forecast data
Forecast -> Forecast: Calculate actual sales and\nexponential moving-average forecast
Forecast --> User: Display actual and forecast sales
@enduml

@startuml
title JKsur+ Sequence 8 - Ask Inventory and Expense Assistant

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #222222
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #777777
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444444
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8E8F0
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #222222

actor "Admin" as User
participant "AI Assistant View" as Chat
participant "Store Context" as Store
participant "Gemini API Endpoint" as Endpoint
participant "Gemini AI Service" as Gemini

User -> Chat: Enter a question
Chat -> Chat: Check that question is in inventory /\nexpense scope

alt Question is out of scope
  Chat --> User: Display local scope refusal
else Question is in scope
  Chat -> Store: Read inventory and expense data
  Store --> Chat: Prepare current store context
  Chat -> Endpoint: POST prompt and context data
  Endpoint -> Endpoint: Validate prompt and scope
  alt Assistant request succeeds
    alt Gemini API key is configured
      Endpoint -> Gemini: Generate answer with store context
      Gemini --> Endpoint: Answer text
      Endpoint --> Chat: Return answer
    else Gemini API key is not configured
      Endpoint --> Chat: Return live-database summary fallback
    end
    Chat --> User: Display assistant answer
  else Assistant request fails
    Endpoint --> Chat: Return service error
    Chat --> User: Display assistant unavailable message
  end
end
@enduml
